meta {
  name: Presign Quote Document
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/quote-recaps/quote-document/presign
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "leadId": "{{createdLeadId}}",
    "filename": "carrier-quote.pdf",
    "contentType": "application/pdf",
    "size": 2048
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Feeds the raw PUT (seq 3) and then the create (seq 4).
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("quoteDocumentKey", res.getBody().key);
    bru.setVar("quoteDocumentUploadUrl", res.getBody().uploadUrl);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("returns a presigned PUT scoped to the agency and lead", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("key");
    expect(body).to.have.property("uploadUrl");
    expect(body.requiredHeaders).to.have.property("Content-Type");
    expect(body.key).to.contain("/quote-recaps/");
    expect(body.expiresIn).to.be.a("number");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /quote-recaps/quote-document/presign — upload URL for the carrier quote (PAC-39)

  Issues a short-lived presigned PUT so the browser uploads the quote document
  **directly to object storage**. File bytes never pass through the API, and no
  base64 data URL is ever stored.

  - **Module:** `quote_recaps`
  - **Permission:** `quote_recaps:write`
  - **Data scope:** `own` — presigning against another producer's lead **404s**.

  ## Body
  | field       | type   | required | rules                                        |
  |-------------|--------|----------|----------------------------------------------|
  | leadId      | string | yes      | 24-char Mongo ObjectId; ownership is checked first |
  | filename    | string | yes      | 1–255 chars; sanitized into the key          |
  | contentType | string | yes      | **`application/pdf` only** (PAC-56 #9)       |
  | size        | number | yes      | positive integer, ≤ 10 MB                    |

  ## Behaviour worth knowing
  **PDF only, since PAC-56 #9.** `image/jpeg` and `image/png` used to be accepted
  here; ~98% of carrier quotes are PDFs and photographed quotes mostly arrive
  unreadable. This is a **write-path** rule only — recaps that already hold a
  JPEG or PNG still download and open normally, because
  `GET /quote-recaps/:id/document/download` presigns whatever content type is
  stored. There is no migration and no backfill; do not "clean up" those records.
  The sold-form and deal-audit uploads deliberately still accept images
  (PAC-56 #22) — see `Deal Audits/Presign Audit Attachment.bru`.

  **The edit form calls this endpoint too** (PAC-56 #11). Replacing a recap's
  document presigns here first — the request is scoped by `leadId`, not by recap
  id, so it is the same call the create flow makes.

  **Scoped to the lead, not the recap.** The document is uploaded while the recap
  is still being composed, so no recap id exists yet. The key that comes back is
  `agencies/<agencyId>/quote-recaps/<leadId>/<year>/<uuid>-<filename>`, and
  `POST /quote-recaps` rejects any key that does not carry exactly that prefix —
  which is what stops a caller attaching another agency's object to their own
  record.

  **The `agencyId` in the key comes from the lead document**, never from the
  request, so it cannot be forged.

  **`size` here is advisory.** A presigned PUT signs only `Content-Type`, so a
  caller holding a valid URL could upload something larger. The real enforcement
  is on create, which re-reads type and size from storage via `HeadObject`.

  ## Uploading (step 2 of 3)
  ```
  PUT <uploadUrl>
  Content-Type: application/pdf      # must match requiredHeaders exactly
  <raw file bytes>
  ```
  Send **no `Authorization` header** — any header outside the signature
  invalidates it.

  ## Response `201`
  ```json
  {
    "key": "agencies/665.../quote-recaps/665.../2026/9f2c-carrier-quote.pdf",
    "uploadUrl": "http://localhost:9000/sfa-uploads/agencies/...?X-Amz-Signature=...",
    "requiredHeaders": { "Content-Type": "application/pdf" },
    "expiresIn": 300
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — bad `leadId`, unsupported `contentType`, or `size` over
    10 MB.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `quote_recaps` module disabled, or missing
    `quote_recaps:write`.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such lead, or one outside the caller's data scope.
}
